Short:        OFS/FFS and SFS handlers with TRIM support
Author:       Ilkka Lehtoranta
Uploader:     Ilkka Lehtoranta (ilkleht@gmail.com)
Type:         disk/misc
Version:      1.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 2.0

CopperFS provides new replacement Amiga OFS/FFS and SFS filesystem
implementations with TRIM support. They are written in C# using
GPT 6.1 Sol and 6.0 Astra. The project is MIT licensed.

CopperFFS supports reading and writing DOS0/OFS and DOS1/FFS volumes.
CopperSFS supports SFS and SFS2 volumes. The SFS2 TRST handler also
supports SFS volumes and can recover outstanding CSUN and TRST journals
on writable media.

CopperTrim provides an explicit manual discard command for supported
writable formats and devices. Discard requires a device and driver that
support the required SCSI UNMAP commands.

The release candidate was tested with host and native replay tests and
with original-handler comparisons under emulated Kickstart 3.1. Physical
Amiga and storage testing has not been completed.

Archive contents
----------------

The intended 1.0 archive contains the CopperFFS handler, the CopperSFS
SFS2 TRST handler, the CopperTrim command, this README and the MIT license
and applicable third-party notices. SFS2 TRST is the default CopperSFS
handler and supports both SFS and SFS2 volumes.

Installation
------------

Make a verified backup before changing a partition's filesystem handler.
Complete journal recovery before switching SFS handlers.

Copy handlers to L: on your boot volume. Use CopperFFS for an OFS or FFS
partition, or CopperSFS SFS2 TRST for an SFS or SFS2 partition.
Copy CopperTrim to C: if you want to use it. However, it is only useful
if your underlying device driver supports it.

For a partition configured in the RDB, update the filesystem entry with
the selected handler and assign it to the partition's existing DOS type.
Copying a handler to L: alone does not update an RDB filesystem entry.
For a mountlist or DOSDrivers entry, set its FileSystem field to the handler
in L: and retain the partition's existing device, geometry and DOS type.
Check that the volume mounts and that its files are readable before relying
on it.

After an interrupted SFS write, use the appropriate handler to complete
recovery on writable media before switching handlers. The SFS2 TRST
handler can recover both CSUN and TRST journals.

Source code is at https://github.com/ilehtoranta/CopperFS
